# advisory: none - SQL injection through JSON facet key quoting, found in review
# severity: high
# vector:   a JSON key is telemetry, so whoever can send to dfe-receiver picks
#           it, and every signed-in member loads facets for keys they did not
#           write. mergePath wrapped each JSON segment in backticks without
#           escaping, and passed a segment already in backticks through raw. A
#           key holding a backtick closes the identifier early, and the rest of
#           the key lands raw in getKeyValues' groupUniqArray(N)(...), whose
#           "(" check skips re-quoting, so it runs as the team's ClickHouse
#           user. mergePath now quotes each segment with quoteJsonSegment
#           (dfe/jsonPath.ts), the escape patch 0005 gives quoteJsonPathSegment,
#           and the facet render unescapes a quoted segment before quoting it
#           again, so a key holding a backtick or a backslash, or named like
#           a type hint, still finds its values
#           (dfe/__tests__/facetKeyQuoting.int.test.ts).
# upstream: none - still present on hyperdxio/hyperdx main
# added:    2026-11-28
